'''Ineseño''' ({{Langx|inz|Sʰamala|links=no}}) is an extinct and revitalizing [[Chumashan languages|Chumashan language]] spoken in southern [[California]]. It was closely related to, and may have been a dialect of, [[Barbareño language|Barbareño]]. Ineseño is currently undergoing processes of [[language revitalization]].<ref name=":4">{{Cite web |title=Chumash Culture |url=https://chumash.gov/culture#programs |access-date=2024-09-08 |website=Santa Ynez Band of Chumash Indians |language=en-US}}</ref><ref name=":2">{{Cite news |last=Chawkins |first=Steve |date=2008-04-20 |title=Chumash recover their 'alishtaha'n: Armed with a trove of scattered notes, linguist saves ancestral tongue from brink of extinction. |url=https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-2008-apr-20-me-chumash20-story.html |access-date=2013-05-07 |work=Los Angeles Times}}</ref><ref name="santabarbara">{{Cite web |title=Chumash Dictionary Breathes Life into Moribund Language |url=http://www.independent.com/news/2008/apr/24/chumash-dictionary-breathes-life-moribund-language/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20140508042649/http://www.independent.com/news/2008/apr/24/chumash-dictionary-breathes-life-moribund-language/ |archive-date=2014-05-08 |access-date=2013-05-07 |work=The Santa Barbara Independent}}</ref><ref name=":3">{{Cite web |date=2010-04-08 |title=Bringing Back the Samala Chumash Language |url=https://www.nps.gov/chis/learn/news/bringing-back-the-samala-chumash-language.htm |url-status=live |archive-url=https://archive.today/20130626173631/http://www.nps.gov/chis/parknews/bringing-back-the-samala-chumash-language.htm |archive-date=June 26, 2013 |access-date=2013-05-07 |work=Channel Islands National Park}}</ref> An Ineseño dictionary was published in 2007.<ref>{{Cite book |url=https://www.worldcat.org/title/231862451 |title=Samala-English dictionary: a guide to the Samala language of the Ineseño Chumash People |date=2007 |publisher=Santa Ynez Band of Chumash Indians |isbn=978-0-615-13131-3 |editor-last=Santa Ynez Band of Chumash Mission Indians of the Santa Ynez Reservation, California |edition=1st |location=Santa Ynez, Calif |oclc=231862451 |editor-last2=Applegate |editor-first2=Richard B.}}</ref>

